Parent companion for FPGA-gPTP #84/#85 (rides the next gptp-processor pin adoption).
Applies to milan-fpga dev e9cbb676 with the gptp-processor gitlink at 2022d363
(the RTL and ROM images of 53ac2e9d; only comments and guides changed).
The published path is pathTrace: the received pathSequence plus thisClock
(OUR_CID) appended when it is not empty, so each count gains one entry.

| Line | Expectation | Was | Now | Clause |
|---|---|---:|---:|---|
| 891 | published full path count ([GM, hop, src] + thisClock) | 3 | 4 | IEEE 802.1AS-2020 10.3.9.23 / 10.3.13.2.4 f) 5) |
| 930 | explicit one-entry PathTrace publishes count two ([GM] + thisClock); new tail0 == OUR_CID | 1 | 2 | IEEE 802.1AS-2020 10.3.9.23 / 10.3.13.2.4 f) 5) |
| 943 | present path restored for servo controls ([GM, hop, src] + thisClock) | 3 | 4 | IEEE 802.1AS-2020 10.3.9.23 / 10.3.13.2.4 f) 5) |
| 1003 | better Announce preserves full path count ([GM2, hop, src2] + thisClock) | 3 | 4 | IEEE 802.1AS-2020 10.3.9.23 / 10.3.13.2.4 f) 5) |

